/*
 * Jini Configuration -- Reggie, born-DER instance
 *
 * This configuration file is read by RegistrarImpl via
 * ConfigurationProvider.getInstance(configArgs, classLoader).
 *
 * Component: org.apache.river.reggie
 *
 * Demonstrates the ratified born-immutable format epoch (JGDMS-STD-006
 * sec.3 item 5; SOW-Entry-ATOMIC-DER-Migration.md sec.4 A3): a registrar's
 * marshalling format is a whole-instance property, fixed at instantiation
 * and immutable for the life of the store -- never a per-relationship
 * decision derived from an individual client's own (droppable) method
 * constraints. Setting `useDerForEntries = Boolean.TRUE` below is the
 * *only* thing this config needs to do:
 *
 *   (i)   RegistrarImpl.entryFormat() becomes ATOMIC_DER for this instance
 *         -- covering this Reggie's own self-registered attributes, every
 *         registrant's attribute sets, and every lookup template alike,
 *         all read from this single config entry at startup.
 *   (ii)  RegistrarProxy/Registration/Item carry that format as their own
 *         immutable, non-getConstraints()-derived `entryFormat` field,
 *         populated at construction -- a client ProxyPreparer.setConstraints()
 *         call can never drop or change it.
 *   (iii) The exporter automatically becomes AtomicDerILFactory (instead of
 *         AtomicILFactory) AND the exported proxies' initial method
 *         constraints automatically require MarshallingFormat.ATOMIC_DER --
 *         wire-layer belt-and-braces alongside (ii), so a genuinely
 *         DER-incapable legacy client fails loud with
 *         UnsupportedConstraintException, never a silent mismatch. A
 *         deployer-supplied `serverExporter` entry (as an earlier revision
 *         of this file demonstrated by hand) still overrides this default
 *         entirely, but is no longer necessary just to get DER.
 *
 * A DER-born Reggie serves only DER-capable clients: this is a *distinct
 * deployment* from a legacy JOSS djinn (a JOSS-only client uses the
 * prior-version djinn instead), not a coexistence mechanism -- there is no
 * "mixing formats mid-migration" scenario under the born-immutable model
 * (an earlier revision of this file's comments described exactly that
 * scenario; it is withdrawn, see the SOW's sec.3 item 5 / sec.9.2
 * resolution). "Migration" means redeploying a new born-DER instance and
 * retiring the old JOSS one at the operator's pace, never an in-place flip
 * of a populated store's format (RegistrarImpl's snapshot recovery guard
 * refuses that).
 *
 * NOTE: this is a payload-marshalling-format concern (EntryRep/Item/Template
 * field encoding), layered on top of and orthogonal to
 * qa/harness/configs/der's existing "der" family of configs, which
 * configures the JERI/SSL transport wire protocol (STD-006) -- not
 * addressed by this file.
 */

import net.jini.core.discovery.LookupLocator;

org.apache.river.reggie {

    /*
     * -------------------------------------------------------------------------
     * The whole-instance born marshalling format (JGDMS-STD-006 sec.3 item 5):
     * read once at startup by RegistrarImpl. This one entry drives (i) this
     * Reggie's own self-registered attributes, every registrant's attribute
     * sets, and every lookup template (via RegistrarImpl.entryFormat()); (ii)
     * the immutable entryFormat field every exported RegistrarProxy/
     * Registration/Item carries; and (iii) the exporter's invocation layer
     * factory (AtomicDerILFactory) plus the initial ATOMIC_DER method
     * constraint baked into the exported proxies -- see RegistrarImpl's
     * Initializer and start().
     * -------------------------------------------------------------------------
     */
    useDerForEntries = Boolean.TRUE;

    /*
     * -------------------------------------------------------------------------
     * Discovery: join the "der" group rather than the legacy public ("")
     * group, so that only clients deliberately deployed against this born-DER
     * djinn discover this instance.
     * -------------------------------------------------------------------------
     */
    initialLookupGroups = new String[]{ "der" };
    initialMemberGroups = new String[]{ "der" };

    initialLookupLocators = new LookupLocator[0];

    initialLookupAttributes = new net.jini.core.entry.Entry[0];

    // Uncomment to preserve ServiceID across restarts:
    // persistenceDirectory = "/var/lib/reggie/der";
}
